venus 0115: read only GICv3 distributor and SMMU v5 capability probes

The GPU plan (logs/research/07-gpu-plan.md, Stage B) needs two things the
tree does not have: a GICv3 distributor driver for the GPU interrupt, and
an SMMU for the GPU address space.  Both are too big to guess at, and both
punish a wrong guess: a stray write into GICD_CTLR wedges the interrupt
path of the whole system, and a stray write into the SMMU can lock the GPU
out of memory (or leave a half programmed translation table that the
secure world then has to clean up).

So this patch adds the honest first step: two read only probes.

bsd/dev/sweet_gic.c maps the GICv3 distributor frame (0x17a00000, 64 KiB)
and the redistributor region (0x17a60000, 1 MiB, eight 128 KiB PE frames -
the addresses and the stride come from the live device tree) and prints
the type register, the number of implemented interrupts, the security
state, the LPI support, the number of real redistributor frames, the wake
state of every PE, the enable and pending state of the GPU (SPI 300) and
SMMU (SPI 672..681) interrupts, and the SGI/PPI state of the PE the probe
runs on.  It does not write a single GIC register, and it does not touch
ICC_* - the kernel keeps the Group 1 non secure path that pe_fiq.c sets
up.

bsd/dev/sweet_smmu.c maps the QSMMU v5 ("qcom,qsmmu-v500") global register
window (0x3da0000, 128 KiB), the TCU (0x3dc2000) and the two TBU debug
windows (0x3dc5000, 0x3dc9000) with the two TBU status registers
(0x3dc2200, 0x3dc2208), and prints the revision, the configuration and
identification registers, the number of stream match registers and context
banks, the page table geometry, the fault registers and the TBU state.  It
programs no page table, no stream match register and no context bank: the
device tree says "qcom,skip-init", so the SMMU belongs to the bootloader
and the secure world until there is a real client for it.

Both are off by default:

  sweetgic=1        the GICv3 distributor probe
  sweetgiclpi=1     also read the LPI pending table (maps a RAM page)
  sweet_smmu=1      the SMMU v5 capability probe
  sweet_smmudump=1  also print the stream match registers

The three hunks of this patch sit on lines that the other GPU, haptics and
profiler patches do not use as context (the two file list entries go in
front of the sweet_* group, the two declarations after the include block,
the two calls right after the persistent log is started), so 0115 applies
before and after 0116, 0119, 0121, 0122 and 0124.

The register map, the evidence for every address, what the probes prove
and what a real GICv3 distributor driver and a real SMMU client would
still need are in logs/research/impl/13-gic-smmu-probe.md.

